= Provenance — Simple =

'''Provenance''' is the history of where something came from and what happened to it.

For a painting, provenance can mean who owned it.

For a dataset, provenance can mean:
* where the data came from;
* who collected it;
* how it was changed;
* which software processed it.

For a knowledge claim, provenance can mean which source first made the claim and how later sources copied or changed it.

Provenance helps us check [[Evidence/Simple|evidence]] and understand whether several sources are truly independent.

A citation is part of provenance, but provenance is bigger than a citation.

Provenance also does not prove that something is true. A false claim can have a perfectly clear history.

[[Version control/Simple|Version control]] can provide provenance for files because it records changes over time.

